+    "content": "# Gauge-invariant branch reconstruction and robust discrimination v0.1\n\nDERIVED CONDITIONAL mathematics on the frozen 15-node, 28-link, 18-diamond action. Development lane; independent review PENDING; physical promotion 0. No registry entry.\n\nFor a diamond based at k, define z_d=-psi_k^dagger W_d psi_k/(psi_k^dagger psi_k). This complex scalar is invariant under the full local U(r) gauge group and common matter phase. On the one-active-color embeddings, z_d=exp(i(C theta)_d). In the local phase chart, phi=Arg z=C theta.\n\nWith L=CZ and L^T L=Gamma I, the critical coordinate is EXACTLY b=L^T phi/Gamma on the Lyapunov-Schmidt sheet theta=Zb+y, Z^T D y=0. This holds at every finite rank for these embeddings; it does not classify arbitrary color-normal configurations.\n\nP4=sum b_j^4/(sum b_j^2)^2 equals 1, 1/2, 1/3 on the six balanced, twelve index-one and eight index-two branches. The signed cubic C3=3 sqrt(3) b1 b2 b3/||b||^3 is zero for the first two and +/-1 for the last. Full labeled b distinguishes 26 branches. Real loop and density channels are exactly blind to the opposite overall phase. Six labeled real vertex-loop channels recover squared pair distances in the critical truncation and yield asymptotic class fingerprints 1/4, 1/2, 7/12 on the full branches.\n\nIf the oriented phase error is bounded in Euclidean norm by delta, then e=delta/sqrt(Gamma) bounds critical-coordinate error. e<=||b||/7 guarantees nearest-P4-class discrimination; a directly usable sufficient guard is 8e<=||b_hat||. The proved fingerprint error is <=97/1296<1/12. This bound presumes the local embedded branch model and includes no unbounded systematic error.\n\nFor the stable family, omega_radial^2/omega_angular^2 tends to 1+4 A4/B4=4.746844460896146...; the frequency ratio tends to 2.1787254211800406.... The limit is independent of common clock scaling, N and the critical mass. It is an asymptotic model-conditional prediction, not a new empirical result.\n\n64 exact constructor checks passed, plus 12 full stationary-energy readout fixtures, 32 full-U(r) gauge fixtures and 600 bounded-noise fixtures. Numerical fixtures are synthetic and separate from proof. Published-data screening found methods worth adapting, but no direct branch test in the two screened studies. A physical action/observable correspondence remains open.\n\n# Replay and scope\n\nRead the theorem PDF/TeX, THEOREM_SUMMARY and MEASUREMENT_REQUIREMENTS first. This release inherits the frozen action and critical basis from CBF v0.1; no coefficient or accepted ledger entry is changed.\n\nRun `python verify_observables.py` with Python, SymPy, NumPy and SciPy installed. The source-bound graph, branch and directed-interval helpers are included. No external experimental code is executed. EXACT and NUMERICAL reports are separate. The replay checks algebraic ingredients; the analytic gauge/IFT/noise proofs are in the manuscript. These are constructor checks, not independent review.\n\nMEASUREMENT_REQUIREMENTS_v0.1.json is a proposed design contract; it is not a registered or executed experiment. READOUT_GEOMETRY_v0.1.json exports link and diamond ordering, critical curl matrix and reconstruction map in model coordinates. PUBLISHED_DATA_SCREEN_v0.1.json records a two-study compatibility screen, not an exhaustive search. No experimental samples were downloaded or reanalyzed, and no physical validation is claimed. Physical promotion 0.\n\nLocal theorem neighborhood exists from CBF v0.1 but has no certified numerical radius. Closure and unit-modulus checks are necessary consistency checks, not sufficient to identify this action. Absolute lab time, energy, coefficient mapping, preparation and loss terms require a sourced physical bridge. Real-only data cannot identify the overall phase sign. The mathematical phase-conjugation label is not identified with physical CP.\n\nMissing upstream source Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png was not used. Scope does not establish Standard Model coupling unification, proton decay or magnetic monopoles.\n\nInherited theorem and branch proof: https://unified-dynamics-public.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/papers/#critical-bifurcation-v01 . The current theorem is conditional on its local stationary-sheet hypotheses.\n"
